  "name": "mscse-transfer-cap",
  "description": "An MSCSE student with a completed master's from another university brings twelve credits and may transfer nine (§5.2). The cap was always enforced — the fourth course is refused — but until 2026-09-11 no row said what the cap was, so the student could only find it by going over it. The row is the Ph.D.'s own, with the master's parameter key: ms_transfer_completed_ms_credits_max (9), or transfer_unfinished_ms_credits_max (6) when the prior degree was not finished. Since 2026-09-11 the student’s own “transfer approved” checkbox cannot clear a course the DGS has never reviewed — these Purdue courses have no ExternalCourses row — so the credits are pending, not counted, and the row says so in those words. (Wording: the ADGS decides for MSCSE students — 2026-09-11.)",
